### Register
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Alex",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### Login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### Get current user
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Start learning session
POST http://localhost:3000/api/learning/start
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "topic": "Teach me Binary Search from beginner to advanced"
}

###

### List sessions
GET http://localhost:3000/api/learning
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Get session
GET http://localhost:3000/api/learning/{{sessionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Get current concept
GET http://localhost:3000/api/learning/{{sessionId}}/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Answer checkpoint
POST http://localhost:3000/api/checkpoints/{{checkpointId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "answer": "Binary search requires sorted data because it works by comparing the target with the middle element and discarding the half that cannot contain the target. Without sorted order, we cannot know which half to discard."
}

###

### Ask doubt
POST http://localhost:3000/api/learning/{{sessionId}}/concept/{{conceptId}}/doubt
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "question": "Why does binary search need a sorted array?"
}

###

### Get doubt history
GET http://localhost:3000/api/learning/{{sessionId}}/concept/{{conceptId}}/doubt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Dashboard
GET http://localhost:3000/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Progress
GET http://localhost:3000/api/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Suggested topics
GET http://localhost:3000/api/topics
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/health
